★ [cc-009] Aviation-Inspired AI Incident Reporting: A situation that adapts established aviation safety reporting protocols to the AI regulatory landscape.
Encompasses: Standardized data fields, just culture implementation, and the creation of independent investigation bodies.
  Your interpretation: Skeptics would focus on the difficulty of applying these rules to AI, given the lack of a mature safety culture and the presence of intellectual property barriers that do not exist in the same way in aviation.
  Accelerationist: Accelerationists might view this as a potential source of 'regulatory drag' if the aviation-style bureaucracy is applied too rigidly to fast-moving AI development.
