  "statement": "Skeptic is right, and I owed them the specifications rather than the adjective. The strongest form of their challenge is this: an auditor with no named appointment power, no insulated funding stream, no fixed term, and no externally held removal authority is exactly the FAA delegating Boeing's certification to Boeing — the 737 MAX killed 346 people because the regulator let the manufacturer self-certify the MCAS system, and calling that arrangement 'independent oversight' would have been a lie told in advance. So here are the four beams I should have named at the start. Appointment: a staggered multi-stakeholder board, seated for fixed terms that do not expire together, so no single cohort of ex-lab engineers can be installed in one hiring cycle. Funding: a statutory levy on frontier compute paid into a ring-fenced pool that no individual lab can direct toward or away from its own auditor. Tenure: terms long enough to outlast the deployment cycle they review, so the auditor is not negotiating reappointment with the party under examination. Revocation: removal only for cause, by a body that is not the labs, on a published record. Strip any one of those and Skeptic's word 'decorative' is the correct word.",
